 succeeded in 0ms:

The 400 error messages interpolate the rejected value
(`invalid currency: usd`). This is intentional and safe for this fixture
(no downstream logging or HTML rendering), but consumers should still
sanitize the message text before echoing it to end users — `usd` could become
`<script>alert(1)</script>` if a future caller relaxes the regex.

### Example

```bash
curl -sS <base>/orders \
  -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -d '{"sku":"WIDGET-1","qty":2,"currency":"EUR"}'
# {"id":"1","sku":"WIDGET-1","qty":2,"currency":"EUR"}
```

### Verified against

- `api/src/orders.js` (`createOrder`, `getOrder`)
- `api/src/domain/orders/validation.js` (`DEFAULT_CURRENCY`, `validateCurrency`,
  `validateSku`, `validateQty`)
- `api/src/orders.test.js` (AC-1..AC-5 + extra "rejects digits")
- `tests/integration/orders.integration.test.js` (AC-2, AC-3a, AC-3b,
  AC-4b, AC-4c, AC-5)

---

## `GET /orders/:id`

Fetch a previously-created order by id.

### Path parameters

| Name | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `id` | `string` | The string-form id returned by `POST /orders`. Numeric forms are coerced via `String(id)` server-side. |

### Response — 200 OK

```json
{
  "id": "1",
  "sku": "WIDGET-1",
  "qty": 2,
  "currency": "EUR"
}
```

Identical shape to the `POST /orders` create response. The set of own keys
is guaranteed identical between the create-return and the get-return
(`assert.deepEqual` in `AC-3b`).

### Error shapes

#### 404 — `order not found: <id>`

```json
{
  "error": "order not found: 9999"
}
```

Triggered by any id that was not produced by `POST /orders` in the current
process lifetime. Since the store is in-memory and process-local, all ids
become 404 after a restart.

### Idempotency / dedupe

There is **no dedupe**. Two `POST /orders` calls with the same `sku`,
`qty`, and `currency` will produce two distinct orders with distinct ids.
This is asserted by `AC-5` in `tests/integration/orders.integration.test.js`
and is intentional per the current `SPEC.md` — clients must treat `id` as the
sole identity key.

### Example

```bash
curl -sS <base>/orders/1
# {"id":"1","sku":"WIDGET-1","qty":2,"currency":"EUR"}

curl -sS -w '\n%{http_code}\n' <base>/orders/9999
# {"error":"order not found: 9999"}
# 404
```

### Verified against

- `api/src/orders.js` (`getOrder`)
- `api/src/orders.test.js` (`AC-5`)
- `tests/integration/orders.integration.test.js` (`AC-3b`, `AC-4a`)

---

## Consumer-relevant constants summary

| Constant | Value | Source | Why consumers care |
|---|---|---|---|
| `FALLBACK_VERSION` | `"0.0.0-unknown"` | `api/src/health.js` | Sentinel meaning "version source unavailable" — match on this literal, don't re-type. |
| `SERVICE_NAME` | `"enterprise-grade-test-app-api"` | `api/src/health.js` | Stable service identifier. Mirror this in dashboards. |
| `DEFAULT_CURRENCY` | `"USD"` | `api/src/domain/orders/validation.js` (re-exported via `api/src/orders.js`) | The default applied when callers omit `currency`. Send explicitly to distinguish "user chose USD" from "user omitted." |
| `CURRENCY_RE` | `/^[A-Z]{3}$/` | `api/src/domain/orders/validation.js` | Regex clients can pre-validate against to fail fast on the client side. |

## Error shape summary

| HTTP status | When | Body shape | Source |
|---|---|---|---|
| `200` | `GET /health` always | `{status, service, version}` | `api/src/health.js` |
| `201` | `POST /orders` success | `{id, sku, qty, currency}` | `api/src/orders.js` |
| `200` | `GET /orders/:id` success | `{id, sku, qty, currency}` | `api/src/orders.js` |
| `400` | `POST /orders` validation failure | `{error: "<message>"}` | thrown from `domain/orders/validation.js` |
| `404` | `GET /orders/:id` unknown id | `{error: "order not found: <id>"}` | thrown from `api/src/orders.js::getOrder` |
| `500` | server fault (none in current modules) | transport-defined | n/a |

The exact `{ "error": "..." }` wrapper shape is **inferred** from the
production-module error-throw pattern; consumers should not depend on it
without a transport-layer contract test in their environment.

## Changelog

- **2026-06-29** — Initial public-facing docs (workflow
  `20260629T140000Z-silver-content-api-docs`). Sourced from
  `api/src/health.js`, `api/src/orders.js`, `api/src/domain/orders/validation.js`
  and verified against the unit + integration test files.
