 ## `GET /health`
@@ -310,6 +318,114 @@
 
 ---
 
+## `POST /waitlist`
+
+Create or update a tenant-scoped waitlist entry in SQLite. The endpoint is
+idempotent per `(tenant, email)`: posting the same email for the same tenant
+returns the existing entry id and updates `name` when a non-empty name is
+provided. The same email may exist independently in another tenant.
+
+### Request headers
+
+| Header | Required | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `X-Tenant-Id` | yes | Lowercased and validated against `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{1,62}$`. Invalid or missing values produce 400. |
+
+### Request body
+
+```json
+{
+  "email": "person@example.com",
+  "name": "Person Example"
+}
+```
+
+| Field | Type | Required | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `email` | `string` email | yes | Trimmed, lowercased, max 254 characters. |
+| `name` | `string` | no | Trimmed, nullable, max 120 characters. |
+
+### Response — 201 Created
+
+```json
+{
+  "entry": {
+    "id": 1,
+    "tenantId": "demo-tenant",
+    "email": "person@example.com",
+    "name": "Person Example",
+    "createdAt": "2026-07-06T02:40:00.000Z"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+| Field | Type | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `entry.id` | `number` | SQLite autoincrement id. Stable for duplicate `(tenant, email)` submissions. |
+| `entry.tenantId` | `string` | Normalized tenant id from `X-Tenant-Id`. |
+| `entry.email` | `string` | Normalized email address. |
+| `entry.name` | `string \| null` | Trimmed name or null. |
+| `entry.createdAt` | ISO-like UTC string | Creation timestamp assigned by SQLite. |
+
+### Example
+
+```bash
+curl -sS <base>/waitlist \
+  -H 'content-type: application/json' \
+  -H 'x-tenant-id: demo-tenant' \
+  -d '{"email":"person@example.com","name":"Person Example"}'
+```
+
+### Verified against
+
+- `api/src/waitlist.js` (`WaitlistStore.addEntry`)
+- `api/src/server.js` (`POST /waitlist` transport)
+- `api/src/waitlist.test.js`
+- `tests/integration/waitlist.integration.test.js`
+
+---
+
+## `GET /waitlist/stats`
+
+Return aggregate waitlist stats for exactly one tenant. No cross-tenant totals
+are exposed.
+
+### Request headers
+
+| Header | Required | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `X-Tenant-Id` | yes | Same validation as `POST /waitlist`. |
+
+### Response — 200 OK
+
+```json
+{
+  "tenantId": "demo-tenant",
+  "total": 1
+}
+```
+
+| Field | Type | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `tenantId` | `string` | Normalized tenant id. |
+| `total` | `number` | Count of waitlist rows for this tenant only. |
+
+### Example
+
+```bash
+curl -sS <base>/waitlist/stats -H 'x-tenant-id: demo-tenant'
+# {"tenantId":"demo-tenant","total":1}
+```
+
+### Verified against
+
+- `api/src/waitlist.js` (`WaitlistStore.getStats`)
+- `api/src/server.js` (`GET /waitlist/stats` transport)
+- `api/src/waitlist.test.js`
+- `tests/integration/waitlist.integration.test.js`
+
+---
+
